WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
In 1923, Sigmund Freud pictured
the mind as a rider on a horse.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.430
The horse is stronger.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.900
Often the rider can only guide
it where it wants to go anyway.

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.440
And Freud added a third part of the mind:

5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.100
a stern inner judge that
can make us feel guilty.

6
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.070
So whose voice is guilt,
and should you trust it?

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.240
In this mission, you'll map the
id, the ego and the super-ego,

8
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.960
and set them beside Thomas
Aquinas' very different account.

9
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.530
Then you'll weigh up the case for and
against trusting conscience in real moral

10
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.750
decisions.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.390
Your mission: work out
whose voice guilt might be,

12
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.970
and whether you should trust it.
